''Unlocking GPU Efficiency: Introducing the AIFS Pricing Calculator
AI and HPC workloads are increasingly constrained not by compute, but by data movement and checkpointing overhead. As model sizes grow and checkpoint frequencies increase, a significant portion of expensive GPU time is spent waiting on storage — especially during checkpoint writes.
For many teams, this inefficiency is invisible. It shows up as longer training times, lower GPU utilization, and higher cloud bills — but without a clear way to quantify the root cause.
That’s exactly why we built the AIFS Pricing Calculator.

The Problem: Hidden GPU Idle Time
Modern AI training workloads frequently checkpoint large model states — often in the range of tens of gigabytes — at regular intervals. These checkpoints are critical for:

fault tolerance
long-running training continuity
experimentation and rollback

However, the process of writing checkpoints to backend storage can introduce significant latency. During this time:

GPUs sit idle
training pipelines pause
cluster utilization drops

Even in well-architected environments using high-performance storage, checkpointing can add hours of overhead to large training runs.

The Opportunity: AIFS Acceleration
AIFS (AI File System Accelerator) changes the model by:

absorbing checkpoint writes at NVMe speed
decoupling application-visible latency from backend storage
asynchronously draining data to persistent storage

The result is simple but powerful:

Checkpoint operations complete faster from the application’s perspective, reducing GPU idle time and accelerating overall training completion.


